WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.109
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.109 --> 00:00:02.170
- Most people think

00:00:02.170 --> 00:00:03.853
that owning a parrot is

00:00:03.853 --> 00:00:05.840
a walk in the park, but

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:07.760
the truth is they're very,

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:10.207
very complex creatures in every way.

00:00:10.207 --> 00:00:11.530
They're long-lived;

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:12.430
they can noisy;

00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:13.500
they can be destructive;

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.130
they have special needs;

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:16.210
they challenge you.

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:18.506
Can you say bark like a dog for me please?

00:00:18.506 --> 00:00:19.767
(parrot barking)

00:00:19.767 --> 00:00:22.860
People buy them sometimes
for the wrong reasons,

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:24.023
or they buy on impulse;

00:00:24.023 --> 00:00:27.540
and when there's a problem, they call me.

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:30.123
(upbeat music)

00:00:36.449 --> 00:00:39.030
My name is Glenn Sorino,

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:40.987
and I've been working

00:00:40.987 --> 00:00:43.025
with birds professionally for 20 years.

00:00:43.025 --> 00:00:46.380
New York City has always been my backyard.

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:48.689
I had parakeets growing up as a kid.

00:00:48.689 --> 00:00:51.060
And I was fascinated.

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:52.692
Everything about them appealed to me.

00:00:52.692 --> 00:00:57.232
Eventually, I started to research parrots.

00:00:57.232 --> 00:01:00.470
Read everything I could get my hands on.

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:02.710
Spoke to other bird owners,

00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:03.920
went to bird club meetings

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:06.011
and even took a job at a bird store

00:01:06.011 --> 00:01:08.756
that opened up a lot of doors for me.

00:01:08.756 --> 00:01:11.239
People started calling me.

00:01:11.239 --> 00:01:14.601
"Glenn, I'm having a
problem, can you help me?

00:01:14.601 --> 00:01:16.967
"I thought I had a male parrot

00:01:16.967 --> 00:01:18.832
"but after 20 years it just laid an egg."

00:01:18.832 --> 00:01:23.300
Hello, you name it and the
calls started coming in.

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:25.480
People started flocking to me.

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:27.576
If I can use that term.

00:01:27.576 --> 00:01:31.130
One thing led to another,
and eventually I became

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:34.033
the go-to guy, and it
developed into a business.

00:01:36.132 --> 00:01:40.592
On a day to day basis, I
provide a variety of services.

00:01:40.592 --> 00:01:42.710
I'm there whenever they need me.

00:01:42.710 --> 00:01:44.563
Basically, 24/7.

00:01:44.563 --> 00:01:46.807
Every day is something new.

00:01:46.807 --> 00:01:48.751
Every day is a challenge.

00:01:48.751 --> 00:01:51.670
Each bird has a different behavior.

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:52.630
They're like people:

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:54.210
they have likes, dislikes;

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:56.757
they have special needs
in the way of diet,

00:01:56.757 --> 00:01:58.423
lighting, environment.

00:01:58.423 --> 00:02:01.608
The larger species can
live a human lifespan.

00:02:01.608 --> 00:02:03.710
Owning a bird is literally like having

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:06.090
a 5-year-old child that never grows up.

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:07.500
If you can imagine that.

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:12.160
Bird owners often have
problems with aggression,

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:15.423
health issues, plucking,
egg laying issues,

00:02:15.423 --> 00:02:18.795
mimicking sounds that become incessant.

00:02:18.795 --> 00:02:22.186
(birds chirping)

00:02:22.186 --> 00:02:26.540
I have one client who was
feeding her bird waffles

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:29.868
with maple syrup and
pasta with vodka sauce.

00:02:29.868 --> 00:02:32.170
So we had to change the diet,

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:33.620
and we had to change it fast.

00:02:35.226 --> 00:02:38.559
Every situation presents a challenge.

00:02:38.559 --> 00:02:42.631
My role is to try to help
them through all of that.

00:02:42.631 --> 00:02:46.140
If you understand how a bird thinks,

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:49.020
if you understand what
a bird is telling you

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:50.730
in the way the pupils dilate,

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:52.570
the way they fan their tail,

00:02:52.570 --> 00:02:55.333
you can figure out what
they're trying to tell you.

00:02:56.170 --> 00:02:59.220
I can tell if they're
being cautious at first,

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:01.560
and I approach them very gently.

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:05.290
Again, I speak their
language, and I don't think

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:08.240
there's anyone else who
really does what I do.

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:10.117
You're looking really good aren't you.

00:03:11.423 --> 00:03:16.408
OK, OK Frankie.

00:03:16.408 --> 00:03:18.910
Want to come out?

00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:21.440
I believe that I do have a unique role

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:24.070
in the bird world.
(upbeat music)

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:25.580
I feel the work

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:28.050
that I do is very rewarding to me.

00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:29.210
I love birds.

00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:31.267
I help clients solve problems,

00:03:31.267 --> 00:03:33.640
and when they call me up

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:35.950
and tell me that everything is great,

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:37.270
that I really helped them,

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:38.340
it makes me feel like I'm

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:40.340
really making a difference in the world.

00:03:41.471 --> 00:03:43.580
And I love a happy ending,

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:45.510
and nothing makes me feel better

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:48.233
than knowing that I did a good deed.

